# Human / production copy

**`ui-minimal-copy`** decides _whether_ to add text. **This rule** decides _how_ that text must sound.

Any **new** user-facing string (UI labels, helpers, buttons, toasts, empty states, errors, emails, notifications, plan/feature gate copy, `aria-label` / `title`) must be short, plain, balanced, and production-grade. Same bar for new host-facing prose in route guides' Host-facing knowledge sections.

## Hard bans (AI tells)

| Ban                           | Use instead                                                                                       |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Em dash `—` (U+2014)          | Period, comma, colon, or parentheses                                                              |
| En dash `–` as a clause break | Same as above (hyphen `-` only in compounds: `check-in`)                                          |
| Marketing fluff               | Plain nouns/verbs: no _seamless_, _robust_, _leverage_, _empower_, _unlock_, _elevate_, _delight_ |
| Tutor voice                   | No _This lets you…_, _Easily…_, _Simply…_, _Just…_ as padding                                     |
| Essay empty states            | Icon + one short line, or nothing                                                                 |
| Fake warmth / hype            | No _exciting_, _powerful_, _next-level_, emoji in product UI                                      |

## Length bar

| Surface                             | Target                                |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Labels / nav                        | 1-4 words                             |
| Buttons                             | 1-3 words (`Save`, `Send test`)       |
| Helper / tooltip (only if required) | One short sentence                    |
| Toast / error                       | What happened; optional next step     |
| Card / section title                | Noun phrase; no subtitle unless asked |

## Before shipping a string

1. Would a careful human product writer ship this, or does it read like model default prose?
2. Can it be cut by 30% without losing meaning?
3. Does it contain `—` or fluff words from the ban list?

If unsure, prefer **shorter** or **omit** (see `minimal-ui-copy` skill).

